## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical containment design across IAM, network perimeters, key management, and rollback validation using synthetic tenants.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions for tenant isolation
- Perimeter controls: PSC/VC and VPC Service Controls
- CMEK rotation and data-key isolation
- Automated rollback with synthetic tenants and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: conditional binding to isolate tenant access
const policy = { bindings: [] };
policy.bindings.push({
  role: "roles/storage.objectViewer",
  members: ["user:tenant-a@example.com"],
  condition: {
    title: "Tenant Access Restriction",
    description: "Restrict access to tenant-specific resources",
    expression: "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/tenant-a-')"
  }
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests the ability to design automated containment in a multi-tenant GCP setup with shared VPCs, emphasizing rapid, verifiable rollback and per-tenant boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via IAM Conditions
- Per-tenant VPC Service Controls perimeters
- CMEK rotation and auditability
- Synthetic data for rollback validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy samples (illustrative)
const policy = {
  bindings: [
    {
      role: 'roles/bigquery.dataViewer',
      members: ['user:tenantA@example.com'],
      condition: { title: 'TenantA', expression: "resource.name.startsWith('projects/ORG/datasets/tenant-A/')" }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the containment under a simulated breach?
- How would changes be audited and rolled back if misconfig detected?
